    <!-- InsightsHubScreen -->
    <string name="insights_hub_subtitle">Patterns in your own data: association, not cause.</string>
    <string name="insights_ranked_your_data">Ranked · your data</string>
    <string name="insights_movers_no_overlap">Not enough overlap between your journal answers and %1$s yet. Keep logging. Each behaviour needs days both with and without it before NOOP can read its effect.</string>
    <string name="insights_how_to_read">How to read this</string>
    <string name="insights_how_to_read_body">Everything here is a pattern in your own logged days: an association with an effect size and confidence, never a cause or a diagnosis. Population patterns are shown as “typical” and are always overridden by your own data once you have enough of it. Approximations, not WHOOP’s scores; not a medical device.</string>
